# What the sdist must NOT carry.
#
# setuptools-scm supplies the sdist file list from git, so every tracked file
# is included by default and there is no opt-in list to forget to add to.
# That is the right default for `tests/`, `docs/` and `examples/`, which are
# deliberately shipped: a reviewer of the science should be able to get the
# specification, the examples and the suite from PyPI without a git clone
# (DD-38).
#
# It is the wrong default for `.claude/`. That directory is development
# process machinery: agent charters, skills, the vendored shared-process kit
# and the push-gate hooks. None of it is the library, none of it runs for a
# user, and a hook body inside a published artifact invites someone to run it
# outside the repository it was written for. Author decision 2026-07-30, after
# the release review measured that the v0.2.0 sdist would have carried all of
# it.
#
# `tests/test_release_integrity.py` asserts this over a REAL built sdist, so a
# future change to the build cannot quietly put it back.
prune .claude

# Local staging for proprietary material. Gitignored, so setuptools-scm never
# sees it; pruned here as well because a defense that depends on one mechanism
# is one mechanism away from gone.
prune _private
